    "head_commit":  {
                        "id":  "3260d9e73fec01186891b1403a5e38d6a1d7baa8",
                        "tree_id":  "162624a922f36a73461470be469cf68083947e84",
                        "message":  "fix(deploy): keep the Heroku image in Docker schema2 format (#63)\n\nThe Heroku container registry started rejecting our image with\n\"error from registry: unsupported\" - every layer is pushed successfully, only the\nmanifest upload is refused.\n\nRoot cause (verified by diffing the log of the last successful run with the\nfailing ones):\n\n  run 39269562920 (19/10, success, runner ubuntu-24.04)\n    #16 writing image sha256:16448b85... done          -\u003e Docker schema2 manifest\n\n  run 39627810818 (21/10, failure, runner ubuntu-26.04)\n    #16 exporting manifest sha256:e898b423... done     -\u003e OCI manifest\n    #16 exporting attestation manifest sha256:3618cbe... done\n\n`ubuntu-latest` migrated to Ubuntu 26.04 (runner-image release 20261018.168),\nwhose Docker uses the containerd image store and therefore exports an OCI\nmanifest with an attestation manifest. The Heroku container registry only\naccepts a plain Docker schema2 manifest.\n\nFix:\n- pin the deploy job to ubuntu-24.04 (runner-image 20261012.334, Docker 28.0.4\n  / Buildx 0.38.0) - the exact environment that produced a working push\n- disable the default buildx attestations (--provenance=false --sbom=false) so\n  no attestation manifest is emitted",
                        "timestamp":  "2026-10-22T01:25:50Z",
                        "author":  {
                                       "name":  "Nguyen Van Luan",
                                       "email":  "vanluan.dev@gmail.com"
                                   },
                        "committer":  {
                                          "name":  "GitHub",
                                          "email":  "noreply@github.com"
                                      }
                    },
